    {
      "paperId": "e89661958232cf682ad8416c52fdfc047782cd7e",
      "title": "Real-Time Deep Learning-Based Aerial System for Targeted Pesticide Spraying, irrigation and Crop Disease Detection",
      "abstract": "Agriculture remains the backbone of Rwanda’s economy, yet it faces significant challenges due to inefficient traditional practices, delayed disease detection, and excessive use of inputs like water and pesticides. This project proposes the design and development of a computer vision-based drone system aimed at transforming traditional agriculture into a more efficient, data-driven, and sustainable practice. By leveraging the power of Artificial Intelligence (AI), Internet of Things (IoT), and computer vision, the drone will provide real-time crop monitoring, disease detection, health assessment, and precision spraying capabilities. The system integrates lightweight deep learning models optimized for edge devices to allow onboard, real-time image processing and decision-making. Drawing from proven methodologies such as MobileNet V2, GRU networks, and CNN-DFLC, the solution is tailored to operate under resource constraints common in rural agricultural environments with 98% accuracy. This drone technology will not only minimize pesticide exposure risks and resource wastage but also contribute significantly to national goals such as food security, job creation, and mechanized agriculture as outlined in Rwanda’s NST2 and Agriculture Transformation Strategy. The proposed solution holds promise for scalability and impact across diverse crop types and terrains, making it a vital innovation for Rwanda’s smart agriculture future",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Muyombano Happy Axel",
          "authorId": "2347272905"
        },
        {
